# Boards this example is BUILT AND GATED for.
#
# ★ rt1062 is deliberately NOT listed, even though the example now builds for
# it (`-DEVKB_BOARD=rt1062`, see the board axis in m2_hci_probe.cpp).  Listing
# it would create a gate id `rt1062:networking/m2_hci_probe` whose script
# asserts rt1176-specific lines (`sdio_begin=cmd5-no-response`), and it would
# go red for a reason that has nothing to do with Bluetooth.  The rt1062 build
# is a BENCH configuration, driven by hand, until it has a gate written for it.
#
# ★ AND THE rt1062 BENCH RUN NEEDS TWO HARDWARE REWORKS FIRST, both DNP on the
# MIMXRT1060-EVKB RevB1:
#   R345 -- GPIO_AD_B1_03 -> WL_RST# -> J8.56 (PDn).  Without it the module
#           cannot be power-cycled, so its once-per-power-up ROM greeting can
#           never be caught.  BRIDGED 2026-08-25.
#   R96  -- the CARD->MCU direction: J8.22 -> R18 -> U10 (level shifter) ->
#           R96 -> BT_UART_RXD -> R200 -> GPIO_AD_B1_07.  R200 is fitted and
#           only joins the MCU to an internal net; R96 is what joins that net
#           to the card, and it is NOT fitted.  STILL OPEN.
# Measured with R345 alone: start_inds=0, chip_id=0x0000 -- the MCU can
# transmit to the card and cannot hear it, exactly the pre-R1901 1170 state.
rt1176
